    "body": "## Chat05A first atom (partial, auth-blocked)\n\nAdds a pure, non-routed trigger and stable vote ID contract with regression tests for canonical DRAW, substantive edits, punctuation/whitespace normalization, generated phrase provenance, reload-like repeats, concurrent ID derivation, and invalid battle IDs. The gameplay CI workflow runs this test file.\n\n## Deliberate boundary\n\nNo voting endpoint, worker wiring, participant token reuse, client-supplied viewer ID, persistence insert, NPC, timers, economy, UI, or Cloudflare changes. Current Chat03 Worker authenticates battle-side participants with battle-scoped capabilities; this is not a reliable viewer identity contract. The API remains blocked until a safe spectator identity/auth contract is decided.\n\nThe fixtures establish deterministic candidate IDs only. They do not establish atomic persistent creation or runtime authorization, so this PR is not Chat05A PASS and is not runtime acceptance.\n\n## Validation on exact HEAD\n\n- GitHub Actions at `4f4ff9abf1bb6af25ac0fd36eb6e73a5f9511b48`: `private-api-local`, `sqlite-cas`, `wrangler-local-d1`, and `capture` completed successfully.\n- The Chat05A contract test step and local Worker/D1 integration both completed successfully.\n- Independent `critical_reviewer`: `PASS_STATIC_ISOLATED_SCOPE`; viewer identity, persistent insert idempotency, and runtime authorization remain outside this verdict.\n\n## Base\n\n`main@b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229`",
